   "shape_m": "blockquote",
   "html_text": "Schlick attempts to establish and develop a consistent and completely pure empiricism. … From there, with the help of an analysis of the process of cognition, the Allgemeine Erkenntnislehre first arrives at a clear separation of the rational from the empirical, the conceptual from the intuitional. Concepts are mere signs that are assigned to the world to be cognized; they appear in the ‘statements’ in a very specific order, and these are thus able to ‘express’ certain structures of reality. Ever",
